dist/
docs/*.tmp

# ⚠️ The two watcher logs that used to be ignored here are TRACKED as of 2 Sep 2026.
# The stated reason was "never part of a release" -- but .pkgmeta already excludes the whole
# docs/ folder from the zip, so ignoring them bought nothing and cost the thing that matters:
# a watcher moved to the cloud cannot read or write a file that is not in the repo. The PTR
# watch's first cloud run did all its research and then could not commit a word of it.
# docs/CONTENT_WATCH.md and docs/API_WATCH.md have always been tracked; these two now match.
docs/.writetest_*

# Printable keybind sheets built by tools/keybind_mine.py from one character's
# SavedVariables. Personal output, named after the character, regenerated on demand —
# and MY_KEYBINDS.html is the old fixed name from before the per-character rename.
tools/KEYBINDS_*.html
tools/MY_KEYBINDS.html

# Same idea for tools/profession_plan.py: the sheet lists Rob's own characters and
# realms, so the generator is version-controlled and its output never is.
tools/PROFESSIONS_PLAN.html

# tools/addon_updates.py onthoudt welke addonversies hij vorige keer zag. Beschrijft één pc.
tools/addon_versions_seen.json
# tools/handynotes_watch.py: kopie van HandyNotes_Midnight/zones van de vorige keer. Beschrijft één pc.
tools/handynotes_snapshot/

# De afvinkpagina die tools/testlist_page.py uit docs/TESTLIJST.md bouwt. De generator en
# haar sjabloon staan wél in git; de uitkomst is een kopie van de testlijst en wordt vóór
# elke publicatie opnieuw gemaakt.
tools/testlist_page_build.html

# tools/check_drift.py --seed pakt de locale-bestanden van een oude tag hierheen uit
# om ze door de echte loader te halen. Wegwerp, en volledig af te leiden uit git.
tools/.baseline-*/

# 🧩 The WoW Forever TOC stays OFF GitHub until Rob decides to ship it (night of 5-6 Nov 2026). MEASURED in BigWigsMods
# packager release.sh (v2, lines 1424-1430): it picks up <package>_Camelot.toc when the FILE EXISTS in the checkout and
# tags the release for Forever (1.60.1) — the .pkgmeta ignore list only applies later, when the zip is filled. So a
# tracked-but-ignored Camelot TOC would mark a retail release as Forever while the zip cannot load there.
# The file lives on disk (Rob's Forever folder loads it through the junction); a tracked copy for history is
# docs/forever/MidnightHelper_Camelot.toc.txt — copy it back over when changing either. To ship: remove this line, take the
# file out of .pkgmeta / tools/package.ps1 too (docs/PLAN_FOREVER_RELEASE_2026-11-06.md).
MidnightHelper_Camelot.toc
